From: M1892 mainline project <m1892-mainline@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] input-method-relay: do not dereference destroy signal data

wlroots commit 102a6bd415d4 ("input-method: use `NULL` when emitting
signals") changed the input-method-v2 destroy signals to carry NULL.  The
keyboard grab itself is still reachable through the live input method until
the destroy notification returns, but Phoc continued to interpret the signal
data as the grab and crashed in handle_im_keyboard_grab_destroy().

Use the live grab retained by the input method instead.  This preserves the
existing modifier restoration while following the wlroots destroy-signal
contract.
---
 src/input-method-relay.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/input-method-relay.c b/src/input-method-relay.c
index 85bf7a7..9c10cc4 100644
--- a/src/input-method-relay.c
+++ b/src/input-method-relay.c
@@ -113,7 +113,10 @@ handle_im_keyboard_grab_destroy (struct wl_listener *listener, void *data)
 {
   PhocInputMethodRelay *relay =
     wl_container_of (listener, relay, input_method_keyboard_grab_destroy);
-  struct wlr_input_method_keyboard_grab_v2 *keyboard_grab = data;
+  /* wlroots destroy signals carry NULL. The input method keeps the grab
+   * alive until this notification returns. */
+  struct wlr_input_method_keyboard_grab_v2 *keyboard_grab =
+    relay->input_method->keyboard_grab;

   wl_list_remove (&relay->input_method_keyboard_grab_destroy.link);
